This n8n workflow automates invoice handling from email to reporting. It continuously checks Gmail every minute for new emails that contain **PDF attachments**, 
then collects all attachments, splits them one by one, and uploads each PDF into a selected Google Drive folder for storage. After uploading, it downloads the 
same file again and extracts the text from the PDF. Next, an OpenAI model first checks if the extracted text is actually an invoice (returns only “yes” or “no”). 
If it is **not** an invoice, the workflow deletes the uploaded file from Google Drive to keep things clean. If it **is** an invoice, an AI Agent extracts key 
details like the customer name, company name, invoice amount, and a short description in strict JSON format. Finally, the workflow saves this structured invoice
data into a Notion database and sends a professional email report containing the invoice details to a chosen email address. 

